## Summary

**Device lifetime moved from a global singleton to explicit open-once-and-pipe.**

### `utils.py`
- Removed the `DeviceGetter` singleton class (and its now-unused `import math`).
- Added two functions capturing the same open configuration the codegen used (`(1, 4)` mesh, `FABRIC_1D_RING`, `l1_small_size = 1 << 15`):
  - `open_device(...)` — sets the fabric config and opens the mesh device.
  - `close_device(device)` — closes it and resets the fabric config to `DISABLED` (mirroring the old `__del__` teardown).

### `main.py`
- `main()` and `test_main()` (the two entry points) now each call `utils.open_device()` once, pipe the handle into `load_inputs(device)`, `load_weights_for__main_from_state_dict(device)`, and `_main(..., device)`, and close it in a `finally` (in `test_main` the close happens after the output is pulled back to host).
- `_main(activations, weights, device)` forwards `device` to `consteval__main(ce_cache, weights, device)`.
- `consteval__main(ce_cache, weights, device)` passes `device` to all 48 `main_const_eval_*` calls (verified: 48/48).
- All 48 `main_const_eval_*` functions now take `device` as a parameter; each internal `utils.DeviceGetter.get_device(...)` open was removed and its references repointed to the piped `device` (123 references).

### `params.py`
- `load_weights_for__main_from_state_dict(device)` now takes the device as an argument; removed the internal `get_device` call and the now-dead `MESH_SHAPE`/`FABRIC_CONFIG` constants and `import utils`.

### `activations.py`
- `load_inputs(mesh)` now takes the mesh device as an argument; removed the internal `get_device` call and the now-dead `import utils`.

No `consteval.py` exists (the const-eval functions live in `main.py`), so it was not created. All four edited files parse cleanly, no `DeviceGetter`/`get_device` references remain, and no tests were run.

